WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.815 --> 00:00:06.095
Third time might be a charm, but a fourth entry is&nbsp;
just pushing it when it comes to some film series.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:11.160
Look, "Terminator 3: Rise of the Machines"&nbsp;
can't touch the toes of its predecessors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.700
but it at least tries to tell a follow-up&nbsp;
story that many fans had pondered after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.880
the conclusion of "Terminator 2:&nbsp;
Judgment Day." The critics agreed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.500
with the general consensus being it wasn't the&nbsp;
best film in the franchise but it was decent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.500
hence the 70% critical&nbsp;
approval on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:31.260
Then, "Terminator Salvation" arrived in 2009.&nbsp;
It boasts an all-star cast featuring Christian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:35.820
Bale as John Connor and Sam Worthington as&nbsp;
the cyborg Marcus Wright. The film covers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:41.160
the origin of the T-800 and how the unstoppable&nbsp;
Terminator came to be. Unfortunately, it also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.420
has the distinction of being a "Terminator" film&nbsp;
without Arnold Schwarzenegger, which is basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:49.560
the equivalent of a Batman movie without the&nbsp;
Dark Knight. Fans weren't exactly thrilled that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:53.935
Schwarzenegger's likeness was utilized, but&nbsp;
he failed to make an actual appearance here.

00:00:53.935 --> 00:00:57.660
Even though this was the first "Terminator"&nbsp;
film to truly take the action to the dystopian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.920
sci-fi future that everyone feared, there was&nbsp;
a massive disconnect between this installment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:06.540
the audience, and critics. This soft reboot&nbsp;
of the franchise was a monumental flop,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.720
receiving only 33% critical&nbsp;
approval on Rotten Tomatoes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:14.940
and making around $372 million at the&nbsp;
box office from a $200 million budget.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:19.260
People can say what they want about the&nbsp;
first three "Transformers" films, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:25.800
they were pure money, making over $2.6 billion at&nbsp;
the global box office. That said, diehard fans of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:30.000
the animated series and popular toys always wanted&nbsp;
the story to shift away from the human characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.040
to focus more on the bots and Cybertron's rich&nbsp;
lore. When it was clear that Shia LaBeouf wasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.180
returning for "Transformers: Age of Extinction,"&nbsp;
and trailers showed off the Dinobots in action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:43.301
the audience had their fingers crossed that&nbsp;
the fourth movie might be something different.

00:01:43.301 --> 00:01:48.120
In the end, "Transformers: Age of Extinction"&nbsp;
is essentially the same formula from before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:53.760
with new human characters replacing the previous&nbsp;
archetypes. The story beats were the same. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:59.400
slow-motion scenes were the same. Heck, even the&nbsp;
love story was the same. If this film was made in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:04.200
2023, it would feel as if someone asked ChatGPT to&nbsp;
make a "Transformers" film in the style of Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:09.300
Bay. Despite the cookie-cutter approach, "Age of&nbsp;
Extinction" made over a billion dollars at the box&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:14.280
office, but it also received the lowest critical&nbsp;
and audience scores on Rotten Tomatoes until the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:19.133
follow-up, "The Last Knight." Eventually, the&nbsp;
franchise was rebooted with 2018's "Bumblebee."

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:21.900
"That's a whole can of worms. There's&nbsp;
a million stories I could tell you."

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:26.280
"Superman 4: The Quest for Peace" is a study of&nbsp;
how a singular film can destroy one of the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:30.960
popular franchises in the world. By the time&nbsp;
this movie entered production, there wasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:35.220
really a demand for it. "Superman 3" had seen&nbsp;
a drop in its earnings and critical reception,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:38.734
indicating it might have been a good time&nbsp;
to wrap up the story as a trilogy. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:42.540
The Cannon Group secured the rights to&nbsp;
Superman and convinced Christopher Reeve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.780
to return as the Man of Steel for another&nbsp;
feature in which he had story input.

00:02:45.935 --> 00:02:49.595
Speaking about working with Cannon&nbsp;
to the Los Angeles Times, Reeve said:

00:02:49.595 --> 00:02:53.400
"They're like the guy who flies tourist&nbsp;
and wants first-class service. I admire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.280
their recklessness in buying into&nbsp;
Superman, though they do like to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:00.492
nickel-and-dime you on paper clips. But for&nbsp;
the most part, we're getting what we want."

00:03:00.492 --> 00:03:06.120
Famously, "Superman 4" experienced a tumultuous&nbsp;
production, featuring budget cuts, cheap effects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:10.140
and entire scenes of the movie being&nbsp;
trimmed to keep down the costs. Mark Pillow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:13.920
who played Nuclear Man, explained to Yahoo&nbsp;
how most of his scenes were cut and how he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.480
had a feeling all was not well. In the end,&nbsp;
the film was ravaged by fans and critics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:23.270
sentencing any potential Superman film to&nbsp;
the Phantom Zone for almost two decades.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:26.640
"Home Alone 3" had the smarts to change&nbsp;
characters when it realized Macaulay Culkin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:30.300
took a break from acting, and there was no&nbsp;
chance this feature would lure him out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:35.460
retirement. Was it as good as the previous&nbsp;
entries in the film series? No. But it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:40.034
executes a similar premise under an original&nbsp;
guise and fans accepted it for what it was.

00:03:40.034 --> 00:03:44.040
The made-for-TV "Home Alone 4: Taking Back&nbsp;
the House" thought it could capitalize on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.820
the original series' popularity and return to&nbsp;
the adventures of Kevin McCallister and one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:52.080
his main foes, Marv, in a new flick.&nbsp;
Unfortunately, it recast both roles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:56.760
as Mike Weinberg and French Stewart replaced&nbsp;
Culkin and Daniel Stern respectively. Naturally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:59.700
fans were having none of it and&nbsp;
rejected the film out of principle.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:04.740
What is even more insulting is how "Home Alone&nbsp;
4" tries to recreate the exact same gags from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:09.240
the first two movies. Despite the negative&nbsp;
reaction and general disinterest in this movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:13.740
it didn't stop filmmakers from soldiering&nbsp;
on and making further uninspired sequels.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.860
"Keep the change, you filthy animal."

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:21.240
"The Matrix" has always been a peculiar franchise&nbsp;
in the sense that everyone loved the first film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:25.320
but the sequels weren't as universally&nbsp;
beloved upon release. They weren't hated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:29.040
but one would struggle to find someone&nbsp;
who listed "The Matrix Reloaded" or "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:33.780
Matrix Revolutions" as their favorite in the film&nbsp;
series. Nonetheless, they stood the test of time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:37.740
and most fans tend to look back on them more&nbsp;
fondly now since they wrapped up the story of Neo.

00:04:37.901 --> 00:04:40.121
Considering the conclusive nature of the trilogy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.121 --> 00:04:44.040
eyebrows were raised when it was announced a&nbsp;
fourth movie had entered production and would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:48.540
see the return of Keanu Reeves and Carrie-Anne&nbsp;
Moss. There were questions. But of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:51.868
fans would tune in to see what "The&nbsp;
Matrix Resurrections" was all about.

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:55.380
What followed was one of the most&nbsp;
divisive responses to a "Matrix"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:59.820
film yet. While the critics gave it 63%&nbsp;
critical approval on Rotten Tomatoes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:04.080
audience members were left confused by&nbsp;
what they had seen. The film plays like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:08.340
a meta-commentary on the previous films, while&nbsp;
it seemingly brings back these characters for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:12.840
no good reason other than to continue the story.&nbsp;
"Resurrections" also bombed at the box office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:19.860
only making $157 million from a $190 million&nbsp;
budget. That said, there's a caveat in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:23.880
sense that the world was only emerging from the&nbsp;
coronavirus pandemic's haze, and Warner Bros.'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:28.740
model of dropping cinema releases on HBO Max&nbsp;
on the same day didn't help box office numbers.

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:33.660
Indisputably, Jack Sparrow is the most&nbsp;
iconic character from the "Pirates of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:36.720
the Caribbean" movies; however,&nbsp;
the operative word is "pirates"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:40.140
here. A large part of the franchise's&nbsp;
success to that point had come due to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:44.040
the supporting performances from Will Turner&nbsp;
and Elizabeth Swann. While Captain Jack might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:47.301
have been the main face on the poster&nbsp;
and the character with the best lines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.301 --> 00:05:51.741
Will and Elizabeth were the heartbeat of the story&nbsp;
and brought steadiness to the wild adventures.

00:05:51.741 --> 00:05:55.680
The fourth movie, "On Stranger Tides,"&nbsp;
didn't feature either of them. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:00.120
the two actors declined to return for the movie.&nbsp;
Speaking to The Independent, Kiera Knightley said,

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:04.440
"I said when I finished the trilogy that that was&nbsp;
going to be it. I had a wonderful time on it and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:10.080
I met some extraordinary people but you know,&nbsp;
I think, for me, three is enough, definitely."

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:14.400
While "On Stranger Tides" did feature other&nbsp;
returning characters such as Captain Barbossa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:18.840
it simply lacks the gusto and appeal of the&nbsp;
previous films. The new cast members didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:22.740
possess the chemistry of Will and Elizabeth,&nbsp;
and their absence was sorely felt here.

00:06:23.945 --> 00:06:24.905
"I hate you."

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:29.760
By the time "Shrek the Third" released,&nbsp;
DreamWorks was pushing it. How many times&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:33.120
can an unfriendly ogre, his talking&nbsp;
donkey friend, and other fairy-tale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.500
characters make us laugh until our insides&nbsp;
hurt? Well, the studio had the last laugh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:42.720
as the movie made over $800 million at the global&nbsp;
box office. Regardless of what anyone thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:47.349
of Shrek and its longevity as a franchise, the&nbsp;
families turned up in numbers to watch the movies.

00:06:47.434 --> 00:06:50.640
As revealed by the screenwriter, the&nbsp;
original plan for "Shrek" was to end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:54.120
it after five films. Though this&nbsp;
changed while the team made "Shrek&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:57.300
Forever After," believing it would end&nbsp;
the series on a more conclusive note.

00:06:57.611 --> 00:07:01.211
While the fourth movie did introduce&nbsp;
new characters and different ogres,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.211 --> 00:07:06.420
it was clear the series was on its last legs and&nbsp;
stumbling around aimlessly. The jokes and premises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:11.220
are repetitive, and the movie never feels like it&nbsp;
will surprise the audience in a positive way. All&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:16.620
things considered, it seemed like a wise choice&nbsp;
to end the film series there. However, nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:21.304
is ever sacred in Hollywood, and there have&nbsp;
been talks of more "Shrek" films in the future.

00:07:21.304 --> 00:07:25.920
Tim Burton redefined the possibilities of comic&nbsp;
book movies with the release of 1989's "Batman."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:31.020
He showed how these superhero films could be more&nbsp;
than kid-friendly fodder. However, it was this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:35.220
same devil-may-care attitude that resulted in&nbsp;
him getting the sack and being replaced by Joel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:39.720
Schumacher for "Batman Forever" after his dark&nbsp;
aesthetic in "Batman Returns" failed to sell toys.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:43.980
While it's generally accepted that "Batman&nbsp;
Forever" isn't as good as its predecessors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:49.320
the audiences still had fun with it and it&nbsp;
raked in over $330 million at the box office.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.514 --> 00:07:54.194
Expectedly, Schumacher was given the keys to&nbsp;
the Batcave for the sequel, "Batman &amp; Robin."

00:07:54.194 --> 00:07:58.620
The drama began when Val Kilmer decided he&nbsp;
didn't want to be Batman anymore and departed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:03.000
the project, leaving the door open for George&nbsp;
Clooney to slip into the cape and cowl. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:08.640
the biggest issue was not the change in actors;&nbsp;
instead, it was studio interference. After the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:12.420
financial success of "Batman Forever," the toy&nbsp;
companies and other partners were interested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:16.980
in making as much merchandise as possible out&nbsp;
of the film. This impacted the actual quality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:21.720
as it feels like one giant commercial. The fans&nbsp;
and critics saw right through it, and everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:26.580
lambasted "Batman &amp; Robin." It also killed&nbsp;
any potential Batman movies for eight years.

00:08:26.949 --> 00:08:29.049
"This is why Superman works alone."

00:08:29.049 --> 00:08:32.820
"The Karate Kid" franchise was built on the&nbsp;
chemistry and friendship of Daniel LaRusso&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:37.080
and Mister Miyagi. Even though Mr. Miyagi is no&nbsp;
longer part of the story in the current era due&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:40.920
to the passing of the actor, his influence&nbsp;
and invaluable lessons can be felt in "Cobra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:45.000
Kai" as well. The first three "Karate Kid"&nbsp;
movies established and solidified this bond,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.900
as Daniel and Mr. Miyagi helped each&nbsp;
other in their own unique way. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:52.860
a fourth film titled "The Next Karate&nbsp;
Kid" arrived in 1994 without Daniel.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:56.580
Writing in his autobiography "Waxing&nbsp;
On: The Karate Kid and Me," actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:00.060
Ralph Macchio revealed he was never&nbsp;
asked to return for the film. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.820
he found out the movie was happening&nbsp;
after reading about it in the paper.

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:08.040
In "The Next Karate Kid," Daniel is replaced by&nbsp;
Julie Pierce, played by Hilary Swank as the new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:12.240
lead. Much like the story before, Mr. Miyagi&nbsp;
takes Julie under his wing and teaches her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:17.100
karate. However, the audience and critics didn't&nbsp;
exactly take to this change in a positive manner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:21.780
blasting the derivative formula. While Swank's&nbsp;
performance was praised, the film stinks up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:27.180
the franchise on Rotten Tomatoes with a 7%&nbsp;
critical approval rating and 24% audience score.

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:32.520
Instead of releasing "X-Men 4," 20th Century Fox&nbsp;
chose to focus on a prequel of the franchise's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:36.420
most popular character: Wolverine. The&nbsp;
template for the story was already there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:39.900
in the form of the comic book miniseries&nbsp;
"Origin." All the film would have to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:43.380
is lift from the source material and adapt&nbsp;
it to the big screen and throw in Wolverine.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:48.240
While "X-Men Origins: Wolverine" takes influence&nbsp;
from the comics, it also veers off down a tangent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:52.740
that didn't leave many viewers happy. For one, the&nbsp;
decision to make Sabretooth and Wolverine brothers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:57.120
feels too much like a soap opera twist.&nbsp;
Second, Gambit is introduced in the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:00.660
but he doesn't play nearly enough of&nbsp;
a major role. And finally, there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:04.920
Deadpool. By refusing to give the Merc with a&nbsp;
Mouth a costume and stitching his lips shut,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:09.660
it takes away everything that made the character&nbsp;
popular to begin with. In the years since then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:13.620
Ryan Reynolds' "Deadpool" movies have poked fun at&nbsp;
how the character was treated in this adaptation.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:17.580
There had been plans for a Magneto origin&nbsp;
film in the same vein as "X-Men Origins:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:20.220
Wolverine." However, the&nbsp;
lukewarm reception towards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:23.580
the film and average box office&nbsp;
performance put a pin in the idea.

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:24.840
"What are you doing?"

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:28.680
As an action-horror franchise, "Underworld"&nbsp;
strikes a fine balance between the frights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:32.400
and thrilling spectacle. The third movie,&nbsp;
"Rise of the Lycans," acts as a prequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:35.820
and only features the series' lead&nbsp;
Kate Beckinsale in a cameo at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:39.300
end. After having the missing story&nbsp;
blanks filled, fans were excited to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:43.200
see Beckinsale return in full force as&nbsp;
Selene for 2012's "Underworld: Awakening."

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:48.300
Yet, all the excitement, frenetic energy, and&nbsp;
originality from before had been depleted by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:53.340
the time the fourth movie arrived. Critics gave it&nbsp;
a shallow 25% approval rating on Rotten Tomatoes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:57.180
and many were left questioning what was the&nbsp;
point of continuing the story if it was going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.180 --> 00:11:03.060
to be bland. Another sequel, "Underworld: Blood&nbsp;
Wars," dropped in 2016, but even that couldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:06.540
give the film series the bite it needed&nbsp;
to get back on track to its glory days.

